Dear all,

I have a large phylogeny (625 species). The pdfs produced when I run the analyses and not useful for me since everything is clogged in one page so I'd like to hand pick my nodes of interest (and their range_probabilities) to manually add pie charts (i.e) in these nodes by other means.

In the trtable I can see the daughters nodes for each node. However when I plot the the nodes
plot(tr, label.offset=0.3, tipcex=0.3, statecex=0.3,cex = 0.3)
axisPhylo()
nodelabels()
it's difficult to hand pick the nodes of interest.

​

Is there a way of exporting the tree with the nodes numbers on it, so I can make sure I'm choosing the right nodes? Or any other solution?

Any idea is welcome.

Best for ow,
Boni

​​

--
Esther Nieto
